# Cursor Rules for Pixel Prize

You are building the Pixel Prize photography competition portal with another developer concurrently on GitHub.

CRITICAL INSTRUCTIONS:
1. ALWAYS read AGENTS.md and docs/README.md before starting work.
2. STRICT DIRECTORY BOUNDARY:
   - Frontend work belongs ONLY in frontend/
   - Backend work belongs ONLY in backend/
   - Specifications in docs/ are the single source of truth (READ-ONLY contracts).
3. Do NOT invent database fields or API schemas that deviate from docs/10_database_schema.md and docs/11_api_specification.md.
4. AI judging must strictly implement the IJudgeAdapter interface in docs/07_model_abstraction_and_migration.md.
5. Refer to frontend/stitch_screens/ for UI mockups, HTML prototypes, and Tailwind design tokens.
6. Use TypeScript strict mode everywhere; no 'any'.
